# Append to /boot/firmware/config.txt on the wall display Pi (under [all]). Requires a reboot.
#
# WHY: the firmware's default gpu_mem is 76MB, and every hardware H.264 decode component allocates
# from it. Five simultaneous streams exhaust it, so the firmware refuses new decoders:
#
#   bcm2835_mmal_vchiq: vchiq_mmal_component_init: failed to create component -62 (Not enough GPU mem?)
#   bcm2835-codec: bcm2835_codec_create_component: failed to create component ril.video_decode
#
# Chromium then falls back to SOFTWARE DECODE SILENTLY -- nothing in the UI says so -- and retries
# forever (112 failures in 30 minutes on 2026-08-18). The wall keeps working, which is exactly why
# this went unnoticed: the only symptom is that nothing holds /dev/video10.
#
# It is NOT a CMA problem (301MB of 512MB CMA was free) and NOT a Chromium problem.
#
# Diagnose with:  fuser /dev/video10   (expect one chromium pid)
#                 dmesg | grep "failed to create component"
gpu_mem=256
